{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Basic Elements on Programming", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about programming.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Talk about principles, concepts, and characteristics of general-purpose computer programming language in spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.   Exchanges simple information on principles, concepts, and features of general purpose computer programming languages.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect: Affirmative Form", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <strong>present perfect</strong> to talk about an action that started in the past and is still happening now. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can also use the <strong>present perfect</strong> to talk about an action that is still happening or that stopped recently, but somehow it has an effect on the present. The <strong>present perfect</strong> emphasizes the result of an action as well.<br/><br/>   The structure of the <strong>present perfect</strong> in <strong>affirmative</strong> statements is as follows:<br/><br/>  <center>Subject + have/has + verb in past participle</center><br/><br/>  Examples:<br/><br/>  <span class =\"italic\">Since I started programming, I <strong>have</strong> always <strong>taken</strong> into account the input and output.<br/> She<strong> has</strong> just <strong>finished</strong> writing the event-controlled loop.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Programmers have used keyboards, text files, and touchscreens as ways of entering data into a program.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would rather start by talking about the five basic elements that have made programming possible.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Flowcharts to Present Basic Elements of Programming", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <strong>flowchart</strong> is a drawing that represents the different stages of a process. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use a <strong>flowchart</strong> in programming to diagrammatically represent an algorithm. A workflow shows the steps of a process, which are connected by arrows in order to indicate the sequence of the elements.<br/><br/>  You need to use specific symbols to make a flowchart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01img01.jpg", "type": "image"}, {"content": "Let's check an example of a flowchart that represents the steps of the process of an ATM machine.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01img02.jpg", "type": "image"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "input ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "any kind of data that is entered into a program  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The input is the information that enters into the system and is needed for a program to work. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "arithmetic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the method or way mathematical operations work in a program", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The next element is arithmetic; this has always been the most difficult one, as it is where all the mathematical operations happen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "conditional ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the event that determines when the coding loop stops", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't forget that an important element for the loop is the conditional, which determines when the loop finishes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "looping ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a set of instructions that is repeated a determined number of times", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Deciding what kind of looping you would rather use in order to repeat an operation a certain number of times in the program is an essential part of programming.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "flowchart ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a diagram of the steps in a process", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In this case, you need a flowchart to make sure you are following the right steps in a process.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "event-controlled loop ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a part of a program that determines when the loop ends by introducing an external event ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Would you rather use the event-controlled loop or the counter-controlled loop?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for information about 